WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.829
IEC 62443 distributes cybersecurity responsibility across the industrial lifecycle.

00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:17.937
The asset owner owns or operates the industrial environment and remains accountable for understanding operational risk, defining security requirements, approving residual risk, and sustaining the security program.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:24.146
System integrators and automation solution providers turn requirements into a working architecture.

00:00:24.146 --> 00:00:33.574
They select and configure components, define zones and conduits, establish accounts and communication paths, test controls, and deliver documentation.

00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:38.863
Their work must satisfy both cybersecurity objectives and process requirements.

00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:44.152
Product suppliers develop hardware and software used in industrial systems.

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:55.420
They are responsible for secure development practices, documented capabilities, vulnerability handling, update information, and clear assumptions about how a product should be deployed.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:02.089
A product's capability is useful only when the system design uses it correctly.

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:07.838
Service and maintenance providers preserve or modify the system after commissioning.

00:01:07.838 --> 00:01:15.887
Their remote access, tools, credentials, change practices, and incident communication become part of the security architecture.

00:01:15.887 --> 00:01:25.775
Contracts and operating procedures should define what access is permitted, how it is approved, and what evidence must be retained.

00:01:25.775 --> 00:01:29.684
Shared responsibility does not mean vague responsibility.

00:01:29.684 --> 00:01:38.653
Projects should assign ownership for risk decisions, configuration, accounts, patching, backups, monitoring, incident response, documentation, and end-of-life planning.

00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:43.942
Handoffs between suppliers, integrators, and operators are common failure points.

00:01:43.942 --> 00:01:53.830
Acceptance criteria should verify that required controls work and that the asset owner receives the information needed to operate them.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:02:00.499
Security is strongest when every role understands both its obligations and its dependencies.

00:02:00.499 --> 00:02:09.927
No participant can transfer all risk to another party, and no single participant can manage the entire lifecycle alone.
